WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
At human scale, thyroid eye disease
begins with questions

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.550
that can cross specialties
and complicate care.

3
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.150
Move closer, and the orbit reveals
a layered environment of muscle,

4
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.400
fat, connective tissue, immune cells,
and orbital fibroblasts.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.640
Closer still,

6
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.740
signaling at the cell membrane becomes
part of a much larger biological picture.

7
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.450
One pathway under investigation is

8
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.700
insulin-like growth factor one
receptor signaling.

9
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.550
Linsitinib is an investigational
oral small molecule

10
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.360
being studied in relation
to IGF-1R signaling.

11
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.560
No single model tells the whole story.
That is why Sling Therapeutics is bringing

12
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.250
experienced clinicians together
to examine the evidence,

13
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.020
challenge assumptions,
explore unmet needs,

14
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.900
and identify the questions
that matter most in practice.

15
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.740
Join the conversation.
Bring your experience.

16
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.800
Help shape the questions.

17
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.780
Linsitinib is investigational and
not approved as a marketed product.
